jitReturnMidT -- SEQ 394 R3 (Tony): a handed-over return MID-BODY, with a statement after it whose effect would show.
rmY is a field carrying its code, so `return rmY;` is a bare read of a list (S6) and is handed to run time; `rmAfter = 99;`
follows it. rmT is compiled and takes the call's value into rmV. The interpreted twin (this file with `jitter;` deleted):
RM-1 46, RM-2 0. On jit-list-handover before SEQ 393 A's cure: RM-1 99, RM-2 99 -- the return ran interpreted, the
compiled function went on, rmAfter was written and its 99 became the function's value. This file carries Stroke A's H7.
